# Epic research pipeline (orchestrator-only parent)

When the user requests the full epic pipeline (research → brainstorm → design → adversarial → register → compose), the **parent thread orchestrates only**. Subagents produce all substantive artifacts.

## Phase order (strict gates)

| Phase | Subagent(s) | Gate before next |
|-------|-------------|------------------|
| a. Research | `recon` ∥ `librarian` (+ NLM / praxia search / WebSearch) | Research note path exists |
| b. Brainstorm | contemplex facilitator → critic → synthesizer | `brainstorm_finalize` spec written |
| c. **Design** | **`staff`** | **Design doc + child DAG slugs exist** |
| d. Adversarial | **`spec-challenger` ∥ `spec-defender`** (read-only) | **Both spec AND design passed in** |
| d′. Reconcile | **`staff`** (or `fixer` for surgical edits) | BLOCKER/MAJOR resolved in spec+design; MINOR → fix or `debt` |
| e. Register | **`staff`** | Backlog epic + children with all fields |
| f. Compose | **`staff`** or `planner` | Sprint TOML by wave → `dw emit-sprint` → `orch_session` queue |

**Never run phase d in parallel with phase c.** Adversarial critique requires the staff design artifact.

## Parent MAY do

- `workspace_handshake`, `transduction_log` / phase logging with stable `task_id`
- Launch subagents; paste inputs; collect handoffs
- Gate transitions (FAIL → re-dispatch staff/planner)
- `git commit` when user asks and outcome audit approves

## Parent MUST NOT do

- Edit spec, design, research notes, sprint TOML, or product code
- Call `backlog add` / `backlog update` directly (delegate to **staff**)
- Patch spec during adversarial review (delegate **staff** reconcile)
- Skip staff design before adversarial review

## Violations (learned #2180)

- Parent edited spec + registered backlog + wrote sprint TOML → **wrong**
- Challenger/defender launched parallel with staff design → **wrong order**
